{"kind":"stack","id":"s-light","title":"Light and seeing: 5 questions, 2 flash cards and a story","theme":{"background":"#fdfbf4","foreground":"#222222","font":"Georgia, serif"}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c1-q","content":"What do we need in order to see things?"},{"type":"button","id":"c1-a","label":"Light","why":"Light travels from a source to our eyes, so we can see things.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c1-b","label":"Sound","why":"Pupils may mix up senses; sound lets us hear, not see.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c1-c","label":"Cold air","why":"Pupils may think feeling cold helps us notice things; it does not help us see.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c2","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c2-t","content":"Light"},{"type":"text","id":"c2-e","content":"Light is what lets us see. It comes from sources like the sun, lamps and screens."},{"type":"button","id":"c2-n","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c3","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"image","picto":"sun"},{"type":"text","id":"c3-q","content":"Which of these is a natural source of light?"},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a","label":"The sun","why":"The sun makes its own light, so it is a natural source.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-b","label":"The moon","why":"The moon only reflects sunlight, so pupils often think it makes light.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-c","label":"A mirror","why":"A mirror reflects light but does not make it.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c4","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c4-q","content":"What is dark?"},{"type":"button","id":"c4-a","label":"The absence of light","why":"Dark is what we have when there is no light reaching our eyes.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-b","label":"A kind of light that is black","why":"Pupils may think black is a light; dark is only the lack of light.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-c","label":"Light that is too bright to see","why":"Pupils may think very bright light causes darkness, when it is the lack of light that makes dark.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c5","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c5-t","content":"You are in a room and the lights go out. You need to find your bag. What do you do?"},{"type":"button","id":"c5-a","label":"Wait for your eyes to adjust","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c5-b","label":"Find a torch or a lamp","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c6","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c6-t","content":"Your eyes adjust a little, but the room is still too dark. Without light, you cannot see your bag."},{"type":"button","id":"c6-n","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c7","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c7-t","content":"The torch lights up the room, and you find your bag quickly. Light helps you see."},{"type":"button","id":"c7-n","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c8","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c8-q","content":"Why could you not see your bag in the dark room?"},{"type":"button","id":"c8-a","label":"There was no light reaching your eyes","why":"Without light reaching our eyes, we cannot see things.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c8-b","label":"Your bag was too heavy to see","why":"Pupils may think weight affects seeing; it does not.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c8-c","label":"Your eyes were closed","why":"Pupils may think closed eyes are the reason; in the story, the eyes were open but there was no light.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c9","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c9-t","content":"Dark"},{"type":"text","id":"c9-e","content":"Dark is what we have when there is no light. It is the absence of light."},{"type":"button","id":"c9-n","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c10","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"image","picto":"bulb"},{"type":"text","id":"c10-q","content":"Which of these is a human-made source of light?"},{"type":"button","id":"c10-a","label":"A lamp","why":"A lamp is made by people and gives out its own light.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-b","label":"A cup","why":"A cup does not give out light, so pupils may pick it by mistake.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-c","label":"A stone","why":"A stone reflects light only, so it is not a source.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c11","kind":"end","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c11-h","content":"Well done: you finished the light and dark lesson!"},{"type":"text","id":"c11-m","content":"Light helps us see, and dark is the absence of light. Keep noticing light around you."}],"actions":[]}}
